## Run

You need [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/); it installs the Python version pinned in `pyproject.toml`.

```bash
uv sync
uv run streamlit run src/{{ package_name }}/app.py
```

Or press F5 in VS Code; `.vscode/launch.json` starts the same command under the debugger. The app opens at http://localhost:8501 and shows the stack behind this project, read from `uv.lock`: how many packages are locked, which are direct runtime or development dependencies, which are transitive, and which packages the most others depend on.

## Test and check

```bash
uv run pytest              # unit tests per layer, plus a Streamlit AppTest run of the page
uv run pytest --cov        # the same with coverage
uv run ruff check --fix .  # lint, and fix what it can
uv run ruff format .       # format
uv run pyright             # type-check src/ in strict mode
```

## Layout

```text
src/{{ package_name }}/
├── app.py                 # the page: widgets and layout, nothing else
├── adapters/lockfile.py   # I/O: reads uv.lock and returns validated models
├── models/                # Pydantic models; StackFilter validates what the widgets send
└── services/inventory.py  # pure functions: classify, filter, summarize
tests/{{ package_name }}/                       # unit tests per layer
tests/integration/{{ package_name }}/test_app.py   # drives the page with Streamlit's AppTest
Dockerfile, .dockerignore, scripts/             # container build and push
```

The base template also contributes `notebooks/`, `.vscode/`, and `.gitignore`{% if sample_module %}, plus `src/{{ package_name }}/module.py` with its test because `sample_module` was answered yes{% else %}, plus `tests/{{ package_name }}/test_import.py`, which checks that the package imports{% endif %}.

## Make it yours

Keep the layering and swap the contents. Point `adapters/` at your data source and return models from it, describe that data in `models/`, put the computation in `services/` as pure functions with unit tests, and keep `app.py` to widgets and layout. The `StackFilter` model shows the pattern for validating widget values before they reach any logic.

## Container

```bash
./scripts/build-container.sh                    # builds {{ project_slug }}:local
docker run -p 8501:8501 {{ project_slug }}:local
./scripts/push-container.sh{% if 'azurecr.io' not in container_registry %} --namespace <owner>{% endif %}  # tags and pushes to {{ container_registry }}
```

{% if 'azurecr.io' in container_registry -%}
The push script signs in to Azure Container Registry with `az acr login`, so you need the Azure CLI and an `az login` session with push rights. No namespace is needed for Azure.
{%- elif container_registry in ('ghcr.io', 'docker.io') -%}
On `{{ container_registry }}` the namespace is your user or organization. Sign in once with `docker login {{ container_registry }}`, or set `REGISTRY_TOKEN` and the script signs in for you. Pass `--registry` to push somewhere else.
{%- else -%}
The script assumes an existing `docker login {{ container_registry }}` session; `--namespace` is optional and, when given, becomes the path segment before the image name. Pass `--registry` to push somewhere else.
{%- endif %}

The scripts are Bash; on Windows run them from WSL2. They use `docker` directly when your user can reach the daemon and fall back to `sudo docker` otherwise.

## Dependencies

```bash
uv add polars                   # runtime dependency
uv add --group dev hypothesis   # development-only dependency
```

Both commands update `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`. Commit both files together; the page reads `uv.lock`, so it reflects the change on the next run.

### Package index

{% if package_index_url -%}
This project resolves packages from `{{ package_index_url }}`, set by the `[[tool.uv.index]]` block in `pyproject.toml`, not from PyPI. Anyone running `uv sync` needs access to that index. Credentials come from the machine's uv configuration (a `uv.toml` with an index credential or the `keyring` provider), never from this repository. The container build passes the same index to `uv sync` as a build secret; `scripts/build-container.sh` explains what it needs.
{%- else -%}
Packages resolve from PyPI. To use a private index, add a `[[tool.uv.index]]` block to `pyproject.toml`; uv's documentation on indexes covers credentials.
{%- endif %}

